  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts most people are referring to are typically called the **Columbia PFG Terminal Tackle** shirts (long-sleeve tee style). Here's a breakdown of the most popular thin/lightweight PFG options:\n\n1. **PFG Terminal Tackle Shirt** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. Equipped with Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, it dries quickly and manages moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n2. **PFG Bahama II Shirt** \u2013 Featuring angler-friendly details and lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun so you can stay out there longer.\n\n3. **PFG Tamiami Long Sleeve Shirt** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric, UPF 50 sun protection, hidden mesh-lined vents in the back, and an antimicrobial treatment that helps reduce odor.\n\n4. **Tidal Deflector / Terminal Deflector** \u2013 If you get hot and sweaty on the water, this is one of the best fishing shirts for cooling, made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology that uses touch-activated cooling fabric to prevent overheating.\n\nThe PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style. The **Terminal Tackle** and **Bahama** styles are the most commonly associated with that thin, lightweight feel people love.",
